---
import PublicLayout from '../layouts/PublicLayout.astro';
---

<PublicLayout
  title="Code of Conduct | St. Paul's Mission Hospital"
  description="The professional and ethical code of conduct expected of all staff, contractors, and volunteers of St. Paul's Mission Hospital."
  canonicalPath='/code-of-conduct'>
  <section class='border-b border-[var(--color-border-soft)]'>
    <div class='max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 sm:px-10 pt-20 sm:pt-28 pb-12 sm:pb-16'>
      <p
        class='text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.28em] text-[var(--color-brand)] mb-5'>
        Professional standards
      </p>
      <h1
        class='text-[2rem] sm:text-4xl font-black tracking-[-0.025em] leading-[1.1] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-6'>
        Code of conduct.
      </h1>
      <p class='text-[15px] text-gray-600 leading-[1.75]'>
        This code applies to all employees, contractors, interns, and volunteers
        of St. Paul's Mission Hospital. It reflects our commitments to patients,
        one another, and the communities we serve.
      </p>
      <p class='text-[12px] text-gray-400 mt-4 italic'>
        Effective date: 1 January 2026 · Version 1.0
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class='bg-white'>
    <div class='max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 sm:px-10 py-16 sm:py-20'>
      <div class='prose-legal'>
        <h2>1. Purpose and scope</h2>
        <p>
          St. Paul's Mission Hospital exists to provide compassionate,
          high-quality healthcare grounded in the healing ministry of Christ.
          This code establishes the professional and ethical standards expected
          of everyone acting on behalf of the hospital. It applies across all
          departments, shifts, and locations, and to all forms of interaction
          with patients, families, colleagues, partners, and the public.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Respect for patients and their dignity</h2>
        <p>
          Every patient is treated with dignity, respect, and compassion,
          without discrimination on the basis of ethnicity, religion, gender,
          age, disability, marital status, socio-economic background, or any
          other characteristic. Staff shall:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Provide care that is clinically appropriate, timely, and respectful.
          </li>
          <li>Protect patient privacy and confidentiality at all times.</li>
          <li>Obtain informed consent for clinical interventions.</li>
          <li>
            Listen to patients and involve them in decisions about their care.
          </li>
          <li>Never subject any patient to abuse, neglect, or humiliation.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. Professionalism and integrity</h2>
        <p>
          Staff shall conduct themselves with honesty, diligence, and
          accountability. Specifically:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Attend work as scheduled, dressed appropriately, and fit for duty.
          </li>
          <li>
            Follow clinical protocols and professional standards of your cadre.
          </li>
          <li>
            Do not accept bribes, kickbacks, or any form of improper inducement.
          </li>
          <li>
            Do not use your position for personal gain or to obtain undue
            advantage.
          </li>
          <li>
            Report errors, near-misses, and adverse events promptly and
            honestly.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>4. Confidentiality and data protection</h2>
        <p>
          All patient, staff, and institutional information is confidential.
          Staff shall not access, discuss, share, or transmit such information
          except as required for legitimate clinical or administrative purposes.
          Personal data shall be handled in accordance with the Kenya Data
          Protection Act, 2019, and hospital policy. Confidential information
          must never be shared via personal email, personal devices, or social
          media.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Workplace conduct and collaboration</h2>
        <p>
          We are one team. Staff shall treat colleagues with courtesy,
          cooperation, and respect. The hospital does not tolerate:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Harassment, bullying, or intimidation of any kind.</li>
          <li>
            Discrimination in recruitment, promotion, or daily interaction.
          </li>
          <li>
            Substance abuse on duty or reporting to work under the influence.
          </li>
          <li>Violence, threats, or aggressive conduct.</li>
          <li>
            Gossip that damages the reputation of colleagues or the institution.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>6. Conflicts of interest</h2>
        <p>
          Staff must avoid situations where personal, financial, or family
          interests conflict — or appear to conflict — with the interests of the
          hospital. Any potential conflict must be disclosed in writing to your
          supervisor or the Human Resources Department. This includes outside
          employment, business relationships with suppliers, and financial
          interests in partner organisations.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Stewardship of resources</h2>
        <p>
          Hospital assets — including equipment, supplies, medicines, funds,
          vehicles, and time — are entrusted to us for the service of patients.
          Staff shall use them responsibly, avoid waste, and never remove
          hospital property without authorisation.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Safety and infection prevention</h2>
        <p>
          Every staff member is responsible for their own safety and the safety
          of those around them. This includes strict adherence to infection
          prevention and control protocols, proper use of personal protective
          equipment, safe handling of sharps and hazardous materials, and prompt
          reporting of incidents.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Reporting concerns</h2>
        <p>
          Staff who witness or suspect a breach of this code are expected to
          report it. Reports may be made to your supervisor, to Human Resources,
          or through the confidential whistleblower channel available from the
          Human Resources Department. Good-faith reporting is protected;
          retaliation against a reporter is itself a breach of this code.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Disciplinary consequences</h2>
        <p>
          Breaches of this code may result in disciplinary action, up to and
          including dismissal, and — where applicable — referral to the relevant
          statutory or professional authority. The nature of the response will
          be proportionate to the seriousness of the breach.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Review</h2>
        <p>
          This code is reviewed periodically by the Hospital Management Team and
          the Board of Management. The current version supersedes all previous
          versions.
        </p>

        <p class='legal-note'>
          For questions about this code, contact the Human Resources Department
          at
          <a href='mailto:recruitment@spmh.co.ke'>recruitment@spmh.co.ke</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</PublicLayout>

<style>
  .prose-legal h2 {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin: 2.25rem 0 0.75rem;
  }
  .prose-legal h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .prose-legal p {
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: #4b5563;
    margin: 0.75rem 0;
  }
  .prose-legal ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding-left: 0;
    margin: 0.75rem 0;
  }
  .prose-legal ul li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.35rem;
    margin: 0.5rem 0;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: #4b5563;
  }
  .prose-legal ul li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.6rem;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--color-brand);
  }
  .prose-legal a {
    color: var(--color-brand);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .legal-note {
    margin-top: 2.5rem !important;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border-soft);
    font-size: 13px !important;
    color: #6b7280 !important;
  }
</style>
